I always do it that way -- dig down on a fountain near my main stash,
then wade into the water to dilute stuff.

It is actually safer then #dipping, not only because of nasty fountain
effects, but also because acid never deals damage that way.

All potential bad side effects are preventable:
1) You could forget to take off and drop rustables, or to wear them
again.
2) If you don't bag or Elbereth-protect stuff, a xorn could eat your
armor, artifacts,...
3) If monsters move onto all adjacent squares while you are in the
water, you drown. Watch those bats in the wizard quest.
4) If you can teleport, you will usually try before crawling out.
Bathe on a non-teleport level or deplete your power with something
useful, first.
5) The digging process can drown your pets. At least you don't break
pacifist.
6) Successfully digging down on a fountain angers the mine town watch
no matter what. Use your pets on the watchmen, and make the captain
follow you to a different level, first. Alternatively, lock them up in
a useless shop.


